This directory exists to turn ON trycmd's filesystem sandbox for versioning.trycmd.

trycmd enables the sandbox for a `.trycmd` file iff a sibling `<name>.out/` exists
(trycmd-0.15.11 src/schema.rs:104 — `fs.sandbox = Some(path.with_extension("out").exists())`).
A `<name>.toml` does NOT configure a `.trycmd` file; it is a test file in its own right, so it is
silently ignored. With the sandbox on, the walkthrough runs against a COPY of `versioning.in/`.

Why it matters here: `tessera init repo` + `tessera commit` build a version history inside the
fixture dir. Run in-place that history ACCUMULATES across runs, so the SECOND `cargo test` saw
`tessera log` print every previous run's versions, failed the walkthrough, and cancelled the other
49 tests in the binary. CI never saw it (the nix sandbox starts clean), so it read as flakiness.

`.keep` is ignored by trycmd, so this directory asserts nothing about the output — it only flips
the sandbox on. Add real expected files here if you ever want to assert on the resulting tree.
